W: 2. I have got a fishpond, my own dearest jewel,
W: Where all my fine fishes do play,
W: And if you comes a-fishing when fishing's in season,
W: I'll tell you, love, how to proceed,
W: You bring your nets with you, your rod in your hand,
W: Your hooks and your angles all at your command,
W: When you throws in all the fishes will play,
W: It's down to the bottom, and that's the right way.
W:
W: 3. I have got a warren, my own dearest jewel,
W: Where all my fine rabbits do play,
W: And if you comes a-ferreting when ferreting's in season,
W: I'll tell you, love, how to proceed,
W: You bring your dog with you, your ferret in your hand,
W: Your spade and your nets all at your command,
W: And the ferret will bolt and the rabbits will play,
W: For it's down to the bottom, and that's the right way.
W:
W: 4. I have got a park, my own dearest jewel,
W: Where all my fine deers I do keep,
W: And if you comes a-hunting when hunting's in season,
W: I'll tell you, love, how to proceed,
W: You bring your dog with you, your nag in your hand,
W: All saddled and bridled all at your command,
W: When the deers they will prowl and the dogs they will brawl,
W: It's then "Gee up, Dobbin!" and back they will fall.
W:
W: (To the second half of the tune on the last verse:)
W: Oh! some do like hunting and some do like game,
W: And shooting a pheasant is gentlemen's game,
W: But fishing in a fishpond is all my delight,
W: Go down to the bottom, you're sure to be right.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_8cb24868.abc

