W:1. In South Australia I was born. Heave away! Haul away!
W:In South Australia 'round Cape Horn, We're bound for South Australia.
W:
W:(Chorus:)
W:Haul away, you rolling kings. Heave away, haul away!
W:Haul away, you'll hear me sing: We're bound for South Australia.
W:
W:2. As I walked out one evening fair
W:'Twas there I met miss Nancy Blair.
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:3. I shook her up I shook her down
W:I shook her round and round the town.
W:W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:4. There aint but one thing grieves my mind
W:To leave miss Nancy Blair behind.
W:W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:5. As we wallap round Cape Horn
W:You'll wish to God you'd never been born
W:W:(Chorus:)
