W:2. It is the choice time of the year
W:For the violets now appear
W:Now the rose receives its birth
W:And the pretty primrose decks the earth
W:
W:[Chorus]
W:Then to the Maypole haste away
W:For 'tis now our holiday
W:Then to the Maypole haste away
W:For 'tis now our holiday
W:
W:3. Here each bachelor may choose
W:One that will not faith abuse
W:Nor repay, with coy disdain
W:Love that should be loved again
W:
W:[Chorus]
W:
W:4. And when you well reckoned have
W:What kisses you your sweetheart gave
W:Take them all again, and more
W:It will never make them poor
W:
W:[Chorus]
W:
W:5. When you thus have spent your time
W:And the day be past its prime
W:To your beds repair at night
W:And dream there of your day's delight
